nce. The clinic signature is shown in blue, rad signature in orange, and nomogram in green.)/K 0/P 864 0 R/Pg 106 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj888 0 obj<</BBox 889 0 R/Height 475.767/O/Layout/Width 243.609>>endobj889 0 obj[175.975 270.879 419.584 746.646]endobj890 0 obj<</A 891 0 R/ActualText(Two ROC curve graphs compare the performance of different models using AUC values. The top graph shows Clinic Signature \(magenta line, AUC 0.844\), Rad Signature \(dotted black line, AUC 0.789\), and Nomogram \(cyan line, AUC 0.897\). The bottom graph di\splays similar comparisons: Clinic Signature \(AUC 0.726\), Rad Signature \(AUC 0.785\), and Nomogram \(AUC 0.889\). Both graphs plot Sensitivity versus 1-Specificity.)/Alt(Two ROC curve graphs compare the performance of different models using AUC values. The top graph shows Clinic Signature \(magenta line, AUC 0.844\), Rad Signature \(dotted black line, AUC 0.789\), and Nomogram \(cyan line, AUC 0.897\). The bottom graph di\splays similar comparisons: Clinic Signature \(AUC 0.726\), Rad Signature \(AUC 0.785\), and Nomogram \(AUC 0.889\). Both graphs plot Sensitivity versus 1-Specificity.)/K 0/P 864 0 R/Pg 93 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj891 0 obj<</BBox 892 0 R/Height 333.411/O/Layout/Width 205.285>>endobj892 0 obj[195.137 413.235 400.422 746.646]endobj893 0 obj<</A 894 0 R/ActualText(Two decision curve analysis graphs for the LightGBM model show net benefit versus threshold probability. Both charts depict the model \(blue line\), treat all \(solid black line\), and treat none \(dotted line\). The model's net benefit is highlighted in \pink, peaking around a threshold probability of 0.4 to 0.6, before declining.)/Alt(Two decision curve analysis graphs for the LightGBM model show net benefit versus threshold probability. Both charts depict the model \(blue line\), treat all \(solid black line\), and treat none \(dotted line\). The model's net benefit is highlighted in \pink, peaking around a threshold probability of 0.4 to 0.6, before declining.)/K 0/P 864 0 R/Pg 81 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj894 0 obj<</BBox 895 0 R/Height 389.424/O/Layout/Width 237.43>>endobj895 0 obj[179.036 357.222 416.466 746.646]endobj896 0 obj<</A 897 0 R/ActualText(Horizontal bar chart showing coefficients for various features. wavelet_LLL_firstorder_MinimumŽ has the highest positive coefficient, while wavelet_LHL_firstorder_RootMeanSquaredŽ has the highest negative coefficient. Other features include wavelet_LLH\_ngtdm_ContrastŽ and log_sigma_5_0_mm_3D_gldm_LargeDependenceHighGrayLevelEmphasis.")/Alt(Horizontal bar chart showing coefficients for various features. wavelet_LLL_firstorder_MinimumŽ has the highest positive coefficient, while wavelet_LHL_firstorder_RootMeanSquaredŽ has the highest negative coefficient. Other features include wavelet_LLH\_ngtdm_ContrastŽ and log_sigma_5_0_mm_3D_gldm_LargeDependenceHighGrayLevelEmphasis.")/K 0/P 864 0 R/Pg 68 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj897 0 obj<</BBox 898 0 R/Height 198.539/O/Layout/Width 414.538>>endobj898 0 obj[90.4819 548.107 505.02 746.646]endobj899 0 obj<</A 900 0 R/ActualText(Two plots illustrating regularization in regression analysis. The top plot is a coefficient path plot showing the coefficients of ten features as lambda increases. The coefficients converge to zero as lambda increases. The bottom plot is a mean squared er\ror \(MSE\) plot with error bars for various lambda values. MSE decreases and then stabilizes as lambda increases. Both plots mark lambda at 0.0295 with a vertical dashed line.)/Alt(Two plots illustrating regularization in regression analysis. The top plot is a coefficient path plot showing the coefficients of ten features as lambda increases. The coefficients converge to zero as lambda increases. The bottom plot is a mean squared er\ror \(MSE\) plot with error bars for various lambda values. MSE decreases and then stabilizes as lambda increases. Both plots mark lambda at 0.0295 with a vertical dashed line.)/K 0/P 864 0 R/Pg 56 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj900 0 obj<</BBox 901 0 R/Height 344.749/O/Layout/Width 215.32>>endobj901 0 obj[190.091 115.767 405.411 460.516]endobj902 0 obj<</A 903 0 R/ActualText(Composite medical images displaying an MRI scan on the left, with a red-highlighted area indicating a region of interest. The right shows a CT scan, providing a detailed cross-sectional view of the abdominal area.)/Alt(Composite medical images displaying an MRI scan on the left, with a red-highlighted area indicating a region of interest. The right shows a CT scan, providing a detailed cross-sectional view of the abdominal area.)/K 0/P 864 0 R/Pg 39 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj903 0 obj<</BBox 904 0 R/Height 133.909/O/Layout/Width 406.035>>endobj904 0 obj[94.7338 612.737 500.768 746.646]endobj905 0 obj<</A 906 0 R/ActualText(Medical imaging showing two cross-sectional scans of the pelvic area and a 3D model in the center. The left image highlights a structure in red within the scan. The right image is a CT scan showing internal organs. The 3D model in the middle is depicted i\n red with intersecting blue lines.)/Alt(Medical imaging showing two cross-sectional scans of the pelvic area and a 3D model in the center. The left image highlights a structure in red within the scan. The right image is a CT scan showing internal organs. The 3D model in the middle is depicted i\n red with intersecting blue lines.)/K 0/P 864 0 R/Pg 29 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj906 0 obj<</BBox 907 0 R/Height 103.635/O/Layout/Width 413.121>>endobj907 0 obj[91.2189 113.669 504.34 217.304]endobj908 0 obj<</A 909 0 R/ActualText(Flowchart depicting the selection process for cervical cancer cases from 2013 to 2018. Initially, 1,654 cases were collected. After applying inclusion criteria, 176 cases remained. Inclusion criteria required histopathological confirmation, MR examination\, and specific treatment protocols. Exclusion criteria included advanced cancer stage, non-evaluable images, presence of other tumors, or prior treatment. Ultimately, 118 cases met both criteria, with 83 designated for the training group and 35 for the te\sting group.)/Alt(Flowchart depicting the selection process for cervical cancer cases from 2013 to 2018. Initially, 1,654 cases were collected. After applying inclusion criteria, 176 cases remained. Inclusion criteria required histopathological confirmation, MR examination\, and specific treatment protocols. Exclusion criteria included advanced cancer stage, non-evaluable images, presence of other tumors, or prior treatment. Ultimately, 118 cases met both criteria, with 83 designated for the training group and 35 for the te\sting group.)/K 0/P 864 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj909 0 obj<</BBox 910 0 R/Height 329.386/O/Layout/Width 382.677>>endobj910 0 obj[106.413 104.655 489.09 434.041]endobj911 0 obj<</Author(Nan Jiang)/CreationDate(D:20251004094716+08'00')/Keywords(chemoradiotherapy; locally advanced cervical cancer; clinical outcomes; machine learning; DWI)/ModDate(D:20251004094716+08'00')/Subject(Jiang N, Ping X, Meng Q, Liu Y, Wang X and Hu C \(2025\) Development, validation, and visualization of a novel nomogram for predicting clinical outcomes of radiotherapy combined with chemotherapy in locally advanced cervical cancer. Front. Oncol. 15:16689\71. doi: 10.3389/fonc.2025.1668971)/Title(Development, validation, and visualization of a novel nomogram for predicting clinical outcomes of radiotherapy combined with chemotherapy in locally advanced cervical cancer)>>endobjxref
